WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:04:21.743 --> 00:04:26.998
(High Valyrian)

3
00:04:32.295 --> 00:04:33.630
What?

4
00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:39.636
I can't understand.

5
00:04:51.064 --> 00:04:52.565
Speak plainly.

6
00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.614
Stop.

7
00:05:00.156 --> 00:05:01.491
Stop it.

8
00:05:33.565 --> 00:05:34.858
- There's been a raven.
- There's been a raven.

9
00:05:39.988 --> 00:05:41.490
Good morrow. Your Grace.

10
00:05:42.574 --> 00:05:45.077
Slept well. I trust?

11
00:05:45.953 --> 00:05:47.829
As I said. there's been a raven.

12
00:05:50.791 --> 00:05:54.044
Aegon's army departed
King's Landing a fortnight ago.

13
00:05:54.169 --> 00:05:59.049
The castles of Rosby and Stokeworth
have both fallen without siege.

14
00:05:59.508 --> 00:06:01.176
They have raised Aegon's banner

15
00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:04.805
and added their levies
to Ser Criston Cole's host.

16
00:06:05.848 --> 00:06:07.683
Both houses cited that

17
00:06:08.559 --> 00:06:11.979
sad business with the usurper's son
in their declarations.

18
00:06:13.147 --> 00:06:14.773
Ser Criston's army

19
00:06:15.482 --> 00:06:17.276
now tripled in strength

20
00:06:17.985 --> 00:06:20.195
might have Harrenhal
as its destination.

21
00:06:20.988 --> 00:06:24.074
Even if you can raise
a host of Rivermen

22
00:06:24.199 --> 00:06:26.785
they will not be ready
in time to face him.

23
00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.878
Let's see what your Lord Paramount
is made of.

24
00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:43.511
M-M-My prince...

25
00:06:43.594 --> 00:06:44.970
M-My grace.

26
00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.347
Your Grace.

27
00:06:47.681 --> 00:06:50.893
Lord Grover is looking more hale
and healthy than I expected.

28
00:06:51.018 --> 00:06:53.437
This is Ser Oscar Tully.
grandson to Grover Tully.

29
00:06:53.521 --> 00:06:55.064
He is heir to Riverrun

30
00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:57.733
and the future Lord Paramount
of the Riverlands.

31
00:06:58.276 --> 00:07:01.779
His Grace. the King Consort.
Daemon Targaryen.

32
00:07:01.862 --> 00:07:04.448
- It is an honor. Your Grace.
- Indeed.

33
00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.707
How fares your grandsire?

34
00:07:17.086 --> 00:07:19.839
Sadly. he remains incapacitated.

35
00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.925
He lies in a kind of waking sleep

36
00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:26.012
unable to do much more
than take meager drink.

37
00:07:26.637 --> 00:07:28.681
It is barely enough to sustain him.

38
00:07:29.265 --> 00:07:30.767
So. he's alive?

39
00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:33.227
Yes. gods be good.

40
00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:36.189
Well. my time is short
and I have need of an army.

41
00:07:36.272 --> 00:07:38.483
Perhaps you might place
a feather pillow over his head

42
00:07:38.566 --> 00:07:40.526
and speed along your inheritance?

43
00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:46.407
I love my grandsire. like a father.

44
00:07:47.242 --> 00:07:50.620
My own lord father died suddenly.
himself a young man.

45
00:07:51.496 --> 00:07:54.040
Lord Grover raised me in his stead.

46
00:07:54.123 --> 00:07:55.500
All very touching.

47
00:07:55.583 --> 00:07:57.377
Are you here to speak
with your grandsire's voice?

48
00:07:57.627 --> 00:07:59.504
For House Tully and the Riverlands?

49
00:07:59.671 --> 00:08:01.089
While he still lives?

50
00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:07.053
- That is not our way.
- Then you're of no use to me.

51
00:08:08.388 --> 00:08:09.931
I can see why the Blackwoods
and the Brackens

52
00:08:10.015 --> 00:08:11.266
did not fear to start a war

53
00:08:11.349 --> 00:08:13.309
beneath the nose
of their liege lords.

54
00:08:13.727 --> 00:08:15.812
House Tully is a fish with no head.

55
00:08:16.104 --> 00:08:19.858
Remind me which of your countrymen
claim to fight in the name of Aegon?

56
00:08:19.941 --> 00:08:22.152
Was it... was it Bracken
or Blackwood?

57
00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:24.738
It was House Bracken
that declared Green. Your Grace.

58
00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.156
Who could remember.

59
00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.283
Summon the Blackwoods here.

60
00:08:28.366 --> 00:08:31.077
I require men of action
to lead my host of Rivermen.

61
00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.566
M'lady.

62
00:09:05.195 --> 00:09:08.156
"Princess."
if we're holding to formalities.

63
00:09:09.032 --> 00:09:11.326
Apologies. Princess.

64
00:09:13.162 --> 00:09:15.038
And you are Alyn.

65
00:09:15.372 --> 00:09:17.457
Yes. Princess.

66
00:09:19.042 --> 00:09:21.795
I'm given to understand
my lord husband owes you his life.

67
00:09:25.883 --> 00:09:28.761
But I was not told
his savior was so comely.

68
00:09:30.054 --> 00:09:32.139
Your mother must've been
very beautiful.

69
00:09:32.348 --> 00:09:33.599
Rhaenys.

70
00:09:42.316 --> 00:09:44.485
- Is your work finished?
- No. m'lord.

71
00:09:55.704 --> 00:09:57.665
I just had a word with your captains.

72
00:10:00.126 --> 00:10:03.504
He was the sailor who plucked you
from your watery grave?

73
00:10:11.053 --> 00:10:12.388
Yes.

74
00:10:13.639 --> 00:10:15.391
You did not think to mention it?

75
00:10:16.225 --> 00:10:17.977
I did not think it relevant.

76
00:10:20.271 --> 00:10:22.189
I know who he is. Corlys.

77
00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:27.069
Alyn's past is no fault of his.

78
00:10:28.279 --> 00:10:29.447
He saved his lord's life.

79
00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.949
He should be raised up and honored.
not hidden beneath the tides.

80
00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:33.576
Is this why you came?

81
00:10:35.119 --> 00:10:36.787
To subject me to an inquisition?

82
00:10:39.081 --> 00:10:42.502
I came to tell you that Baela
has called me to Dragonstone.

83
00:10:42.919 --> 00:10:44.253
Baela?

84
00:10:45.296 --> 00:10:47.882
That council is going to dine on her
and Jace for supper.

85
00:10:47.965 --> 00:10:50.301
They grow restless
in Rhaenyra's absence.

86
00:10:50.426 --> 00:10:53.471
Still. where has that woman gone?

87
00:10:53.554 --> 00:10:56.599
I suspect to try and draw us all
back from the abyss.

88
00:11:19.205 --> 00:11:22.625
- Good morrow. Your Grace.
- Good morrow. Grand Maester.

89
00:11:26.212 --> 00:11:27.547
As requested.

90
00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.384
- I brewed it myself.
- Thank you.

91
00:11:32.552 --> 00:11:34.346
I will see it delivered discreetly.

92
00:11:35.972 --> 00:11:40.226
Do report if the recipient
has need of any remedy.

93
00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:42.562
The tea is known
to disagree with the gut.

94
00:11:43.521 --> 00:11:45.148
I shall observe the girl closely.

95
00:11:52.155 --> 00:11:53.490
Grand Maester.

96
00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.915
You've ever been a practical man

97
00:12:02.249 --> 00:12:04.292
an honorable servant to the crown.

98
00:12:05.544 --> 00:12:08.171
And you served my lord husband
in his darkest hours.

99
00:12:09.172 --> 00:12:10.924
Such was my duty. Your Grace.

100
00:12:12.884 --> 00:12:14.219
Tell me.

101
00:12:16.346 --> 00:12:19.057
Do you believe Viserys wanted
Aegon to succeed him?

102
00:12:23.854 --> 00:12:25.897
I could not know.

103
00:12:27.941 --> 00:12:30.527
His Grace never raised
the matter with me.

104
00:13:30.629 --> 00:13:33.591
Ser Criston Cole's host has taken
to exploiting the tree cover

105
00:13:33.674 --> 00:13:34.884
to conceal its movements.

106
00:13:34.967 --> 00:13:37.720
He now only travels by night
to confound our dragons.

107
00:13:37.803 --> 00:13:39.555
And what is Cole's heading?

108
00:13:39.847 --> 00:13:41.432
It is difficult to say.
but there were signs

109
00:13:41.515 --> 00:13:44.310
of an army moving northwest.
I believe.

110
00:13:44.685 --> 00:13:45.895
She believes.

111
00:13:45.978 --> 00:13:47.730
You should've burned them
when you had the chance.

112
00:13:47.939 --> 00:13:49.190
Perhaps you can. Ser Alfred

113
00:13:49.273 --> 00:13:51.067
when you next sight them
on your dragon.

114
00:13:51.984 --> 00:13:55.821
The only reason we know any of this
is because of Baela's efforts.

115
00:13:55.905 --> 00:13:57.448
What do we know. my prince?

116
00:13:57.657 --> 00:13:59.826
If you ask me. it is little and less.

117
00:13:59.909 --> 00:14:02.578
We know that Cole possesses a host
that is growing in strength

118
00:14:02.662 --> 00:14:03.913
and that it is a problem.

119
00:14:03.996 --> 00:14:06.791
Can Daemon hope to meet it
with his own in time?

120
00:14:06.874 --> 00:14:08.084
And if I know the Riverlands

121
00:14:08.167 --> 00:14:10.128
he has more disentangling
ahead of him

122
00:14:10.211 --> 00:14:13.214
than the end of a Lyseni orgy.

123
00:14:13.423 --> 00:14:16.217
Have you heard word from your father?

124
00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:20.555
No.

125
00:14:20.638 --> 00:14:22.515
Ravens were sent to Harrenhal

126
00:14:22.598 --> 00:14:25.935
seeking news of Daemon's progress
with the Riverlords.

127
00:14:26.019 --> 00:14:28.479
None have. as yet. returned.

128
00:14:28.605 --> 00:14:29.939
Just so.

129
00:14:30.273 --> 00:14:32.609
An enemy host.
growing in constitution

130
00:14:32.692 --> 00:14:37.572
marches somewhere in the vastness
of the Crownlands.

131
00:14:37.655 --> 00:14:40.783
We could. perhaps. act
if only we had a host of our own.

132
00:14:41.201 --> 00:14:42.702
Or someone here to lead us.

133
00:14:43.244 --> 00:14:45.288
Mind your tongue. Ser Alfred.

134
00:14:46.623 --> 00:14:48.792
Does it speak falsely. my prince?

135
00:14:49.042 --> 00:14:51.002
This council is rudderless.

136
00:14:51.544 --> 00:14:53.838
I'm doing my best to steer it.
Ser Alfred.

137
00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:58.968
Why should your voice
be any louder than ours. Princess?

138
00:14:59.094 --> 00:15:00.845
The queen did not name you Hand.

139
00:15:01.054 --> 00:15:03.390
It is her voice.
and that of the king consort

140
00:15:03.473 --> 00:15:06.685
that we need to raise alliances
and command our vassals.

141
00:15:06.768 --> 00:15:09.396
- But they are gone.
- What has come of this council?

142
00:15:14.943 --> 00:15:16.278
My lord.

143
00:15:19.656 --> 00:15:22.409
Our enemy is on the march.

144
00:15:22.993 --> 00:15:24.995
Is there naught to be done
in the absence of the queen

145
00:15:25.078 --> 00:15:28.331
but to grouse and claw for power?

146
00:15:34.421 --> 00:15:36.631
We do not know the queen's doings.

147
00:15:37.966 --> 00:15:42.054
But we must trust that she seeks
the same as each of us at this table.

148
00:15:44.264 --> 00:15:46.183
An end to this conflict.

149
00:16:08.539 --> 00:16:10.332
Men of House Darklyn.

150
00:16:10.999 --> 00:16:13.877
All who bend the knee
to the true king. Aegon

151
00:16:13.961 --> 00:16:15.129
will be spared.

152
00:16:16.213 --> 00:16:18.924
You can earn back your honor
by raising his banner

153
00:16:19.008 --> 00:16:23.053
and fighting in his name
against the Whore of Dragonstone.

154
00:16:24.305 --> 00:16:25.806
All who refuse...

155
00:16:27.766 --> 00:16:29.143
will have their death.

156
00:16:43.824 --> 00:16:45.367
Good morrow. Lord Darklyn.

157
00:16:46.202 --> 00:16:49.038
Is there no honor left
in this world. Cole?

158
00:16:49.747 --> 00:16:53.793
Sacking your queen's own castles
and putting her people to the sword?

159
00:16:54.627 --> 00:16:56.003
"Kingmaker."

160
00:17:00.591 --> 00:17:03.052
You're not fit for the white cloak.

161
00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.975
This is a better death
than a traitor deserves.

162
00:17:09.934 --> 00:17:11.352
You should thank me for it.

163
00:17:14.313 --> 00:17:16.732
Yours will come in kind.

164
00:17:31.789 --> 00:17:33.124
Lord Hand.

165
00:17:48.514 --> 00:17:52.143
We'll lead the van northeast.
follow the coastline.

166
00:17:53.645 --> 00:17:55.396
I realize you were
neither born nor bred

167
00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:58.066
anywhere near the Crownlands.
my good Lord Hand

168
00:17:58.733 --> 00:18:00.944
but Harrenhal is to the west.

169
00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:06.699
Indeed it is.

170
00:18:09.828 --> 00:18:11.162
Fuck you.

171
00:18:11.329 --> 00:18:12.872
I told you
we should've sent our dragons.

172
00:18:12.956 --> 00:18:14.457
And now look what's happened.

173
00:18:15.333 --> 00:18:17.919
Daemon. of all people.
has taken Harrenhal.

174
00:18:18.169 --> 00:18:20.547
I give you a job.
and now you just sit there.

175
00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.215
It's your fucking castle!

176
00:18:24.843 --> 00:18:28.555
Well. that castle is more crippled
than I am. Your Grace.

177
00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:31.558
It's like to drive Daemon to madness

178
00:18:31.641 --> 00:18:32.976
as he attempts to make use of it.

179
00:18:33.059 --> 00:18:34.936
It is beyond his faculties.

180
00:18:36.229 --> 00:18:39.941
It is also penniless.
as I happily control all of its gold.

181
00:18:40.233 --> 00:18:43.653
So. as Harrenhal
saps Daemon's resolve

182
00:18:43.737 --> 00:18:45.947
the false queen remains
trapped on her island

183
00:18:46.031 --> 00:18:49.701
and Ser Criston continues
felling castles in the Crownlands.

184
00:18:52.204 --> 00:18:54.623
I need to be informed of these things

185
00:18:54.873 --> 00:18:56.416
if I am to make informed rulings.

186
00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:59.336
I will not be made to look a fool
in front of my allies and enemies.

187
00:18:59.419 --> 00:19:00.879
Harrenhal must wait.

188
00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:06.969
Ser Criston is marching
on Rook's Rest.

189
00:19:07.719 --> 00:19:09.554
Rook's... A pathetic prize.

190
00:19:09.638 --> 00:19:11.598
- I gave no such command...
- The castle is small

191
00:19:12.933 --> 00:19:14.226
weakly defended

192
00:19:14.559 --> 00:19:17.020
and Lord Staunton
sits on Rhaenyra's council.

193
00:19:17.646 --> 00:19:19.231
After Cole smashes it

194
00:19:19.523 --> 00:19:22.067
we'll have Dragonstone
effectively cut off by land.

195
00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:25.863
This war will not be won
with dragons alone

196
00:19:26.488 --> 00:19:29.450
but with dragons flying
behind armies of men.

197
00:19:29.533 --> 00:19:30.576
No!

198
00:19:30.868 --> 00:19:33.203
Have him turnabout.
I want Harrenhal back.

199
00:19:34.496 --> 00:19:36.540
Cole is already preparing his attack.

200
00:19:38.459 --> 00:19:39.960
How... how do you know this?

201
00:19:40.335 --> 00:19:41.837
He sent word to me.

202
00:19:43.255 --> 00:19:44.590
To you?

203
00:19:46.967 --> 00:19:48.552
The two of you have been...

204
00:19:49.928 --> 00:19:53.807
plotting without my authority?

205
00:20:56.704 --> 00:20:58.581
Harrenhal is a useful morass.

206
00:20:59.082 --> 00:21:01.959
It will keep Daemon well-occupied
while we strengthen our host

207
00:21:02.251 --> 00:21:04.253
and weaken Rhaenyra's
support on the mainland.

208
00:21:04.337 --> 00:21:06.673
We will deal with it
in the Riverlands in time.

209
00:21:07.298 --> 00:21:10.885
But right now.
Rook's Rest is an easy target

210
00:21:11.678 --> 00:21:13.012
and a worthy effort.

211
00:21:14.639 --> 00:21:17.433
Don't you agree. my king?

212
00:21:32.657 --> 00:21:34.033
Come.

213
00:21:38.163 --> 00:21:39.330
Lord Larys.

214
00:21:43.585 --> 00:21:45.462
I thought I'd look in on you.
Your Grace

215
00:21:45.712 --> 00:21:48.340
after your absence
from the small council.

216
00:21:48.757 --> 00:21:50.550
I feared something was amiss.

217
00:21:51.676 --> 00:21:53.595
You're kind to do so. my lord

218
00:21:53.678 --> 00:21:56.222
but indulgence was my sin.

219
00:21:56.306 --> 00:21:59.476
I ventured into the lamprey pie
at last night's supper.

220
00:21:59.559 --> 00:22:01.019
Too far. I fear.

221
00:22:07.943 --> 00:22:09.653
That is a rich indulgence.

222
00:22:11.279 --> 00:22:12.405
But I believe it is a sin

223
00:22:12.489 --> 00:22:14.324
to deny your appetites.

224
00:22:14.825 --> 00:22:17.661
They are what make us fully alive
as mortal men.

225
00:22:22.457 --> 00:22:24.584
Was anything of note
discussed at the council?

226
00:22:25.085 --> 00:22:26.795
Daemon having seized Harrenhal

227
00:22:26.878 --> 00:22:29.464
and His Grace's
resulting displeasure.

228
00:22:29.673 --> 00:22:32.509
I would've thought you would be
the most aggrieved. my lord.

229
00:22:34.636 --> 00:22:36.555
I see it as a loss
for our greater good.

230
00:22:38.432 --> 00:22:40.809
Dragonstone's attentions
are greatly divided.

231
00:22:40.893 --> 00:22:42.519
First in the Riverlands
and the Gullet

232
00:22:42.603 --> 00:22:43.979
and now the Crownlands.

233
00:22:45.022 --> 00:22:46.940
Ser Criston wins every challenge
he faces there.

234
00:22:47.024 --> 00:22:49.943
That truth alone is like to
incite Rhaenyra's fury.

235
00:22:51.236 --> 00:22:53.363
He's covered himself in glory.
to be sure.

236
00:22:54.782 --> 00:22:56.408
And you must worry for him?

237
00:22:57.868 --> 00:22:59.995
Your sworn sword

238
00:23:01.121 --> 00:23:04.249
on the march.
ever exposed to dragons?

239
00:23:04.333 --> 00:23:05.876
It is a perilous road.

240
00:23:09.463 --> 00:23:11.256
Ser Criston is the Hand of the King.

241
00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:15.135
We should all pray for his victory
and safe return.

242
00:23:16.512 --> 00:23:17.846
Indeed.

243
00:23:27.606 --> 00:23:30.484
If I may be so bold. my queen...

244
00:23:36.866 --> 00:23:38.909
you have not seemed yourself of late.

245
00:23:40.870 --> 00:23:43.039
Only weeks ago.
my lord husband was alive

246
00:23:43.205 --> 00:23:44.749
and the realm was at peace.

247
00:23:45.708 --> 00:23:49.337
Now. I've barely had the hours
to grieve one tragedy

248
00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:50.463
before suffering the next.

249
00:23:50.546 --> 00:23:53.257
I regret if I have not been myself.

250
00:23:57.803 --> 00:24:00.514
I did not know you shared
your lord husband's love

251
00:24:01.390 --> 00:24:02.892
for the histories.

252
00:24:04.727 --> 00:24:07.730
If not his love.
then certainly an abiding interest.

253
00:24:09.607 --> 00:24:11.192
The voices of history guided Viserys.

254
00:24:11.275 --> 00:24:14.529
He knew that his wisdom alone
could only reach so far.

255
00:24:14.654 --> 00:24:16.739
Do you think that is why
he changed his mind

256
00:24:18.533 --> 00:24:19.867
in the end?

257
00:24:21.160 --> 00:24:25.039
No matter how suited he thought
Rhaenyra for the crown

258
00:24:25.123 --> 00:24:29.419
the voices of history. as you say

259
00:24:29.752 --> 00:24:33.381
would have told him how the realm
would react to her succession.

260
00:24:33.464 --> 00:24:35.091
It was impossible to know
what steered his thoughts

261
00:24:35.174 --> 00:24:36.509
in those final hours.

262
00:24:38.219 --> 00:24:40.054
Do you now doubt his intentions?

263
00:24:48.104 --> 00:24:50.356
Rhaenyra's supporters
will believe what they wish.

264
00:24:51.316 --> 00:24:52.734
And so will Aegon's.

265
00:24:54.152 --> 00:24:57.530
The war will be fought. many will die

266
00:24:58.740 --> 00:25:01.034
and the victor will eventually
ascend the throne.

267
00:25:03.286 --> 00:25:06.206
The significance of Viserys's
intentions died with him.

268
00:25:13.004 --> 00:25:14.339
Yes. it did.

269
00:26:52.021 --> 00:26:54.607
It's a touch late to be
stalkin' about a strange castle

270
00:26:54.690 --> 00:26:56.400
putting its people to the sword.

271
00:26:56.734 --> 00:26:58.068
You.

272
00:26:59.153 --> 00:27:00.696
I'm called Alys.

273
00:27:01.655 --> 00:27:02.990
Strong?

274
00:27:03.115 --> 00:27:04.450
Rivers.

275
00:27:05.284 --> 00:27:06.619
A bastard.

276
00:27:07.036 --> 00:27:09.288
Once you get to know me.
you'll find I'm not so bad.

277
00:27:10.456 --> 00:27:12.833
So what are you then?
Some kind of... maester?

278
00:27:12.917 --> 00:27:14.377
In a manner of speaking.

279
00:27:14.961 --> 00:27:18.506
I inherited the duties
after the last one fled in the night.

280
00:27:18.589 --> 00:27:21.592
- Fled? Why?
- Just never settled in.

281
00:27:24.345 --> 00:27:25.763
How are you settling in?

282
00:27:27.014 --> 00:27:30.309
I've come to know the face
of tortured rest well enough.

283
00:27:30.768 --> 00:27:34.105
Sleep can be thin in this place.

284
00:27:35.231 --> 00:27:36.774
What would you know of my sleep?

285
00:27:38.443 --> 00:27:41.279
Harrenhal's been cursed
since its first stone was laid.

286
00:27:42.864 --> 00:27:45.116
Black Harren felled
the grove of weirwood trees

287
00:27:45.366 --> 00:27:46.951
that grew on these lands.

288
00:27:47.410 --> 00:27:49.162
Heart trees. imbued with the spirits

289
00:27:49.245 --> 00:27:51.622
of those who lived
long before he came.

290
00:27:51.706 --> 00:27:53.875
It's said their whispers
can still be heard sometimes.

291
00:27:53.958 --> 00:27:55.335
A midwife's tale.

292
00:27:55.752 --> 00:27:58.880
The very bed you sleep in
was made from such a heart tree.

293
00:28:00.840 --> 00:28:04.385
Have you experienced
anything of note?

294
00:28:05.011 --> 00:28:07.096
You are a strange kind of woman.

295
00:28:07.931 --> 00:28:10.391
I'm no woman at all.
I'm a barn owl.

296
00:28:10.600 --> 00:28:12.602
Cursed to live in human form.

297
00:28:15.438 --> 00:28:17.565
So you've come here
after quarreling with your wife?

298
00:28:18.483 --> 00:28:19.692
What?

299
00:28:20.944 --> 00:28:22.570
You arrive here alone

300
00:28:22.695 --> 00:28:25.698
to claim the castle
and yet send no ravens.

301
00:28:28.034 --> 00:28:30.495
Do you now plan
to make your own claim?

302
00:28:31.162 --> 00:28:32.664
Perhaps to prove yourself to her.

303
00:28:32.747 --> 00:28:35.208
Do not try me
with your insolence. witch.

304
00:28:35.291 --> 00:28:36.710
It's a hard thing. I imagine

305
00:28:36.793 --> 00:28:40.255
to give obeisance to one
who replaced you as heir.

306
00:28:43.258 --> 00:28:44.884
And a woman too. A...

307
00:28:45.510 --> 00:28:48.096
girl child you bounced on your knee.

308
00:28:50.557 --> 00:28:53.393
I mean. does it please you
that her legitimacy is contested?

309
00:28:53.476 --> 00:28:57.314
As you stand here.
with a castle and a dragon

310
00:28:58.064 --> 00:29:00.317
attempting to draw an army of men.

311
00:29:05.489 --> 00:29:06.823
Here. Drink this.

312
00:29:08.992 --> 00:29:10.035
You'll need your sleep

313
00:29:10.118 --> 00:29:12.120
if you're to win this place
to your side.

314
00:29:22.297 --> 00:29:25.801
I now rule my house as regent until
my nephew Benjicot comes of age.

315
00:29:31.139 --> 00:29:33.809
The Brackens are venal cravens

316
00:29:34.017 --> 00:29:37.187
and they must pay for their treachery
against the laws of gods and men.

317
00:29:38.939 --> 00:29:40.357
And against the crown.

318
00:29:40.941 --> 00:29:42.276
Who are you?

319
00:29:42.484 --> 00:29:45.404
Ser Willem Blackwood
of House Blackwood. Your Grace

320
00:29:45.529 --> 00:29:46.864
as I said.

321
00:29:51.035 --> 00:29:52.369
Well met.

322
00:29:53.245 --> 00:29:54.747
What might I do for you?

323
00:29:55.039 --> 00:29:58.417
It was you who summoned me.
Your Grace.

324
00:29:59.251 --> 00:30:01.879
I was given to understand that
you wanted an army.

325
00:30:02.463 --> 00:30:04.006
Well. who doesn't these days?

326
00:30:04.298 --> 00:30:06.091
You Blackwoods certainly
never miss a chance

327
00:30:06.175 --> 00:30:09.220
to bloody your swords. do you?

328
00:30:10.387 --> 00:30:13.474
Some 20 years ago.
my lord bent the knee to King Viserys

329
00:30:13.557 --> 00:30:15.226
and acknowledged
the Princess Rhaenyra

330
00:30:15.309 --> 00:30:16.644
as his rightful heir.

331
00:30:16.894 --> 00:30:18.229
So you fight for this old oath?

332
00:30:18.312 --> 00:30:20.356
Not. of course.
for your thousand-year-old feud

333
00:30:20.439 --> 00:30:21.774
with the Brackens.

334
00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:25.486
I once vied for Queen Rhaenyra's hand

335
00:30:26.570 --> 00:30:28.072
before she wed Ser Laenor.

336
00:30:28.989 --> 00:30:30.574
I always liked her spirit.

337
00:30:31.826 --> 00:30:33.703
She had the true blood of the dragon.

338
00:30:33.828 --> 00:30:36.831
And you're prepared to march
without the leave of your lord...

339
00:30:59.854 --> 00:31:01.230
Your Grace?

340
00:31:03.232 --> 00:31:04.942
And once you and your dragon

341
00:31:05.026 --> 00:31:07.445
bring the queen's justice
to the Brackens

342
00:31:08.446 --> 00:31:10.114
our armies will be yours.

343
00:31:19.832 --> 00:31:22.126
Our lords in the Crownlands
are grousing.

344
00:31:22.377 --> 00:31:24.504
Their herds of livestock
struggle to keep pace

345
00:31:24.587 --> 00:31:26.214
with the dragons'
relentless appetites.

346
00:31:26.297 --> 00:31:27.548
Vhagar's in particular.

347
00:31:27.632 --> 00:31:29.467
They can either provide the crown
what it needs

348
00:31:29.551 --> 00:31:31.719
or we can claim their holdings.

349
00:31:31.844 --> 00:31:33.263
Oh. that would be a relief

350
00:31:33.346 --> 00:31:35.640
as we have no more coin
to lend to the effort.

351
00:31:35.723 --> 00:31:38.476
Resources are certainly
growing no more plentiful

352
00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:39.602
in the face of the blockade.

353
00:31:39.686 --> 00:31:41.729
The demand on the blacksmiths.
armorers and tanners for equipment

354
00:31:41.813 --> 00:31:43.898
has only grown apace
with Ser Criston's army.

355
00:31:44.190 --> 00:31:45.984
Well. Cole's done splendidly.
at the least

356
00:31:46.317 --> 00:31:48.236
turning every castle
and army he's faced

357
00:31:48.319 --> 00:31:50.405
including Duskendale.
gods bless him.

358
00:31:51.448 --> 00:31:53.158
The Kingmaker. they're calling him.

359
00:31:53.450 --> 00:31:55.702
And with Aemond and Vhagar
also at the ready

360
00:31:55.785 --> 00:31:57.370
we are a formidable opponent.

361
00:31:59.164 --> 00:32:00.624
You bore me.

362
00:32:03.668 --> 00:32:05.170
You all bore me.

363
00:32:21.728 --> 00:32:25.273
Perhaps Ser Criston will be able
to procure more livestock

364
00:32:25.357 --> 00:32:26.441
through his campaign.

365
00:32:26.525 --> 00:32:29.069
Any coin we can save
will be a welcome bounty.

366
00:32:39.079 --> 00:32:40.122
What are you doing here?

367
00:32:40.414 --> 00:32:41.957
Where are your father's books?

368
00:32:42.165 --> 00:32:43.542
I ordered them removed.

369
00:32:44.042 --> 00:32:46.878
With no thought to the centuries
of knowledge in those pages.

370
00:32:53.468 --> 00:32:54.887
Your Grace.

371
00:32:56.722 --> 00:32:59.224
I removed them. I didn't burn them.

372
00:33:04.605 --> 00:33:05.647
What is it?

373
00:33:06.023 --> 00:33:07.900
They don't care what I think.

374
00:33:11.070 --> 00:33:13.113
- Who. Aegon?
- My council.

375
00:33:13.447 --> 00:33:15.574
Cole. Aemond.
They pursue their campaign

376
00:33:15.657 --> 00:33:17.701
without seeking my aid.
or even my thoughts.

377
00:33:21.080 --> 00:33:22.373
What thoughts would you have?

378
00:33:24.375 --> 00:33:25.709
I'm the king.

379
00:33:29.171 --> 00:33:31.924
Do you think simply wearing the crown
imbues you with wisdom?

380
00:33:38.764 --> 00:33:41.642
Those men at your council table

381
00:33:43.060 --> 00:33:44.520
earned their seats.

382
00:33:46.063 --> 00:33:48.733
It was my hope that once enthroned

383
00:33:49.066 --> 00:33:51.402
you would honor the burden
of your new duties

384
00:33:51.694 --> 00:33:53.028
be silent

385
00:33:53.237 --> 00:33:56.323
and strive to learn from
the more studied minds around you.

386
00:33:58.492 --> 00:34:00.745
In the hope that you might be
half the king your father was.

387
00:34:03.122 --> 00:34:04.999
- Tread carefully.
- Or what?

388
00:34:07.293 --> 00:34:09.670
You'll hang me.
as you did your ratcatchers?

389
00:34:10.338 --> 00:34:12.548
Or have me banished.
as you did your Hand?

390
00:34:14.467 --> 00:34:15.676
I ruled

391
00:34:15.843 --> 00:34:18.137
in your father's absence
throughout his long illness

392
00:34:18.221 --> 00:34:20.932
and Otto Hightower was
as cunning a statesman as ever lived.

393
00:34:21.015 --> 00:34:25.978
You should humbly be seeking
our opinions and counsel.

394
00:34:28.648 --> 00:34:30.566
You have no idea the sacrifices
that were made

395
00:34:30.650 --> 00:34:32.318
to put you on that throne.

396
00:34:37.532 --> 00:34:38.574
Wha...

397
00:34:40.702 --> 00:34:42.495
What would you have me do. Mother?

398
00:34:44.664 --> 00:34:46.541
Do simply what is needed of you...

399
00:34:48.751 --> 00:34:50.044
nothing.

400
00:35:20.408 --> 00:35:21.785
On your feet!

401
00:35:23.703 --> 00:35:25.163
To Rook's Rest!

402
00:35:26.790 --> 00:35:28.124
To battle!

403
00:35:33.505 --> 00:35:35.048
It's broad daylight.

404
00:35:35.423 --> 00:35:38.677
We must hold here and ready ourselves
to lay siege at nightfall.

405
00:35:39.219 --> 00:35:42.180
We shall move now and strike by day.
They will not expect it.

406
00:35:42.430 --> 00:35:45.600
They will not expect it
because it is fucking madness.

407
00:35:48.019 --> 00:35:50.564
Did you forget the little encounter
we had on the road to Rosby?

408
00:35:51.231 --> 00:35:52.566
I did not.

409
00:35:54.401 --> 00:35:56.987
Dragonstone and their dragons
are just across the bay.

410
00:35:58.739 --> 00:36:00.615
What?
Grown tired of living. have you?

411
00:36:01.783 --> 00:36:03.243
Are you afraid. Ser?

412
00:36:04.453 --> 00:36:06.580
Worse. I'm rational.

413
00:36:08.707 --> 00:36:10.125
We advance.

414
00:36:31.188 --> 00:36:32.356
I see no other choice.

415
00:36:32.648 --> 00:36:34.858
- We need to send a dragon.
- Where?

416
00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:43.909
To support the war that your vassals
have been fighting in your absence

417
00:36:44.451 --> 00:36:45.786
Your Grace.

418
00:36:47.037 --> 00:36:50.040
Cole's host has grown
since riding abroad.

419
00:36:50.124 --> 00:36:52.418
He raised the levies
of both Rosby and Stokeworth

420
00:36:52.501 --> 00:36:55.379
and. with their combined strength.
sacked Duskendale.

421
00:36:55.462 --> 00:36:56.922
Duskendale?

422
00:36:57.047 --> 00:36:58.424
The city has fallen.

423
00:36:59.008 --> 00:37:00.676
Many Darklyn men declared for Aegon.

424
00:37:00.885 --> 00:37:02.595
Those who refused
were put to the sword.

425
00:37:02.678 --> 00:37:04.013
What of my father?

426
00:37:04.513 --> 00:37:05.931
He kept his oath.

427
00:37:06.640 --> 00:37:07.725
Cole took his head for it.

428
00:37:10.728 --> 00:37:13.397
Where have you been. these last days?

429
00:37:13.731 --> 00:37:15.816
You vanished
without so much as a word.

430
00:37:16.942 --> 00:37:19.695
Well. I apologize for my absence
and the secrecy

431
00:37:19.987 --> 00:37:21.572
but such was necessary.

432
00:37:22.823 --> 00:37:24.158
I went to King's Landing.

433
00:37:25.952 --> 00:37:27.161
To what possible end?

434
00:37:27.244 --> 00:37:29.789
To meet Queen Alicent
and sue for peace.

435
00:37:29.872 --> 00:37:32.583
- You saw Alicent?
- Yes. I did.

436
00:37:32.708 --> 00:37:34.835
You could've been taken or slain!

437
00:37:34.919 --> 00:37:38.214
I inherited 80 years of peace
from my father.

438
00:37:38.965 --> 00:37:40.258
Before I was to end it

439
00:37:40.591 --> 00:37:42.635
I needed to know
that there was no other path.

440
00:37:46.097 --> 00:37:47.431
And now I do.

441
00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:52.937
Only one choice remains to me.

442
00:37:53.354 --> 00:37:56.607
Either I win my claim or die.

443
00:37:59.193 --> 00:38:00.695
We stand at the ready.

444
00:38:02.322 --> 00:38:04.407
Cole's victories
have only emboldened him.

445
00:38:04.490 --> 00:38:06.326
He marches on Rook's Rest.

446
00:38:06.826 --> 00:38:08.453
His host was just hours away

447
00:38:08.536 --> 00:38:10.288
when Lord Staunton's
ravens took wing.

448
00:38:10.371 --> 00:38:12.874
Why Rook's Rest?
After Duskendale?

449
00:38:13.249 --> 00:38:15.209
It is but a small coastal keep.

450
00:38:15.293 --> 00:38:18.004
'Cause Lord Staunton
is a member of this council.

451
00:38:18.588 --> 00:38:21.090
And because his castle
is small and vulnerable

452
00:38:21.174 --> 00:38:22.509
and there for the taking.

453
00:38:22.759 --> 00:38:25.303
Cole knows we have no army
on the mainland.

454
00:38:25.386 --> 00:38:27.764
- He is brazen.
- He is daring us to act.

455
00:38:27.847 --> 00:38:30.391
We need to send a dragon.

456
00:38:37.732 --> 00:38:41.236
There are those who have mistaken
my caution for weakness.

457
00:38:46.366 --> 00:38:47.909
Let that be their undoing.

458
00:38:49.202 --> 00:38:51.496
- I will go.
- My queen...

459
00:38:51.788 --> 00:38:54.541
- You cannot.
- I will not lose dragons to war

460
00:38:54.624 --> 00:38:55.667
whilst I hide here in my castle.

461
00:38:55.750 --> 00:38:58.962
Our allies raise their banners
for you. Mother.

462
00:38:59.045 --> 00:39:00.380
Yes. they do.

463
00:39:01.089 --> 00:39:03.967
If you die. all is lost.

464
00:39:04.342 --> 00:39:05.510
- Send me.
- No.

465
00:39:05.594 --> 00:39:07.679
I will burn Cole's lines and
withdraw before King's Landing

466
00:39:07.762 --> 00:39:09.556
- could even raise the alarm.
- You lack the experience.

467
00:39:12.642 --> 00:39:15.312
You must send me. Your Grace.

468
00:39:17.147 --> 00:39:20.233
Meleys is your largest dragon
and no stranger to battle.

469
00:39:23.403 --> 00:39:24.946
I will meet Cole.

470
00:40:33.974 --> 00:40:37.520
I wish only to fight for you.
for your claim and mine.

471
00:40:37.728 --> 00:40:39.063
I...

472
00:40:40.690 --> 00:40:42.441
There's something
I need to tell you. Jace.

473
00:40:44.860 --> 00:40:48.114
Something I should've told you

474
00:40:48.322 --> 00:40:50.408
when you first became heir
to the throne.

475
00:40:51.659 --> 00:40:56.455
It's a secret that Viserys told me
when he named me his successor.

476
00:40:57.957 --> 00:41:00.918
And it has passed from king to heir

477
00:41:01.961 --> 00:41:04.255
since Aegon the Conqueror's time.

478
00:41:12.847 --> 00:41:16.893
I never told you because I was unsure
that I believed it myself.

479
00:41:18.227 --> 00:41:21.397
The Targaryen
who sits the Iron Throne

480
00:41:22.148 --> 00:41:24.233
is not just a king or a queen.

481
00:41:24.567 --> 00:41:26.402
They are a Protector.

482
00:41:30.782 --> 00:41:34.327
Ordained to lead the Seven Kingdoms.
to strengthen them

483
00:41:36.913 --> 00:41:40.667
and to unite them
against a common foe.

484
00:41:45.380 --> 00:41:48.383
Viserys chose me to succeed him.

485
00:41:49.801 --> 00:41:51.886
He held to this
the whole of his life.

486
00:41:58.017 --> 00:42:03.356
My father believed that I. alone.
was meant to be this Protector.

487
00:42:04.315 --> 00:42:06.985
They're 1.400. 1.500-strong
at least. my lord.

488
00:42:08.862 --> 00:42:12.282
But to unite the realm.
I had to send the dragons to war.

489
00:42:21.124 --> 00:42:24.211
The horrors I have just loosed
cannot be for a crown alone.

490
00:42:26.838 --> 00:42:28.840
That is why I must believe

491
00:42:28.924 --> 00:42:31.384
what Viserys told me
when he named me his heir.

492
00:42:32.052 --> 00:42:33.887
What Jaehaerys had told him.

493
00:42:35.388 --> 00:42:37.224
And what I will now tell you.

494
00:42:40.227 --> 00:42:41.561
What is it?

495
00:42:47.609 --> 00:42:49.695
Aegon the Conqueror's dream.

496
00:42:52.030 --> 00:42:55.409
He called it
"The Song of Ice and Fire."

497
00:43:05.460 --> 00:43:06.545
Loose!

498
00:43:06.628 --> 00:43:07.754
New rank!

499
00:43:09.089 --> 00:43:10.340
Loose!

500
00:43:10.924 --> 00:43:11.967
New rank!

501
00:43:12.634 --> 00:43:15.512
Loose! New rank!

502
00:43:20.184 --> 00:43:21.226
Push it!

503
00:43:22.019 --> 00:43:23.312
Dragon!

504
00:43:23.395 --> 00:43:25.773
- Dragon!
- Dragon!

505
00:43:30.069 --> 00:43:32.488
To the Seven Hells with you. Cole!

506
00:43:33.155 --> 00:43:35.366
You may as well have sounded horns
to announce our coming!

507
00:43:35.449 --> 00:43:37.409
Order the Darklyn levies
to break off and move ahead.

508
00:43:37.493 --> 00:43:39.328
We must keep
the dragon's attention divided.

509
00:43:39.411 --> 00:43:41.372
- Make the signal.
- What signal?

510
00:43:41.622 --> 00:43:43.165
All is going to plan.

511
00:45:15.508 --> 00:45:17.343
Forward. Sunfyre!

512
00:45:17.969 --> 00:45:19.345
Faster!

513
00:45:20.138 --> 00:45:21.890
- Dragon!
- Dragon!

514
00:45:21.973 --> 00:45:23.058
Whose dragon is that?

515
00:45:23.975 --> 00:45:25.602
His Grace. the king's.

516
00:45:26.686 --> 00:45:28.772
This was your secret plot. Cole?

517
00:45:28.938 --> 00:45:30.690
For the king himself to lay ambush

518
00:45:30.774 --> 00:45:32.859
- and mayhaps die in the attempt?
- No!

519
00:45:32.942 --> 00:45:34.819
Loose more signal arrows!

520
00:45:38.448 --> 00:45:40.909
Stalwart men of House Targaryen

521
00:45:41.826 --> 00:45:44.204
your king has joined you!

522
00:45:45.330 --> 00:45:48.333
Hold to your courage!
Hold to your wits!

523
00:45:48.416 --> 00:45:51.503
For the Seven have blessed
and shielded this host

524
00:45:51.586 --> 00:45:53.046
with divine purpose!

525
00:45:53.338 --> 00:45:56.383
For the one true king. Aegon!

526
00:45:56.591 --> 00:45:59.010
Advance!

527
00:46:07.019 --> 00:46:08.520
Where are you. Aemond?

528
00:46:24.119 --> 00:46:25.662
<i>Dracarys!</i>

529
00:47:04.577 --> 00:47:05.953
Another one there!

530
00:47:06.662 --> 00:47:08.581
Send a volley to those Rosby men!

531
00:47:08.831 --> 00:47:10.749
Give them no quarter!

532
00:47:20.301 --> 00:47:22.136
We'd best get you to cover. my lord.

533
00:48:11.185 --> 00:48:12.729
Thank the gods!

534
00:48:14.314 --> 00:48:15.857
<i>Dracarys!</i>

535
00:48:21.112 --> 00:48:23.448
No! No!

536
00:48:42.759 --> 00:48:44.135
Your Grace!

537
00:53:50.736 --> 00:53:52.529
Fall in behind me!

538
00:53:53.948 --> 00:53:55.533
Into the breach!

539
00:54:27.440 --> 00:54:30.192
The king has fallen.
We must find him.

540
00:55:19.909 --> 00:55:21.286
Aemond!

541
00:55:36.843 --> 00:55:37.886
Where's His Grace?

541
00:55:38.305 --> 00:56:38.733
